          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years</strong><br>\nSigmund Freud was born on May 6, 1856, in Freiberg in Mähren, Moravia, then part of the Austrian Empire, now the Czech Republic. He was the eldest of eight children in a Jewish family and displayed intelligence from an early age, excelling in his studies.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Early Career</strong><br>\nFreud began medical school at the University of Vienna in 1873, showing an interest in neurology. He received his medical degree in 1881 and went on to work at the Vienna General Hospital. His research on the brain's physiology earned him recognition in neurological circles.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Development of Psychoanalysis</strong><br>\nFreud's work with patient studies led him to develop the theory of psychoanalysis. He introduced the idea of the unconscious mind and the significance of dreams in understanding human behavior. His work laid the foundation for modern psychology.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
