          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Legacy and Influence</strong><br>\nFreud's legacy is vast, with his concepts of the id, ego, and superego becoming part of cultural discourse. He is considered the father of psychoanalysis and continues to be a central figure in discussions of therapeutic practice.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Freudian Slip</strong><br>\nThe term \"Freudian slip,\" also known as parapraxis, refers to an error in speech or memory that supposedly reveals subconscious thoughts or desires, another testament to Freud's lasting influence on the analysis of human behavior.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nAfter his death, Freud's ideas have continued to be taught, debated, and developed. His work has had an enduring impact on the fields of psychology, psychiatry, and psychotherapy, with numerous institutions and scholars dedicated to studying his theories.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
